# A workspace with a 0.2 `.mnml/config.toml` and no `.mnml/config.zon`: the
# file is never read (E2), so the statusline shows RESTRICTED and a click on
# the chip (`workspace.review_trust`) says how to convert it — a wrapped toast
# whose instruction reads, not a path-first line clipped at one row on every
# launch (walkthrough 1.10). The statusline chip is what Rust shows there.
write .mnml/config.toml "[ui]\ntheme = \"gruvbox\"\n"
expect screen lacks "RESTRICTED"
command workspace.review_trust
expect screen contains "RESTRICTED"
expect screen contains "export-config-zon"
expect screen contains "is not read"
key esc
expect screen lacks "export-config-zon"
expect screen contains "RESTRICTED"
